        {
          "id": "9395a7c0-9f58-34c4-9e2c-a8c1a06e863a",
          "content": {
            "id": "9395a7c0-9f58-34c4-9e2c-a8c1a06e863a",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "LVMH sales beat on higher China demand sparks luxury share rally",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: LVMH shares jumped to highs of 14% on Wednesday morning, prompting a sector-wide rally.\u00a0</p><p>It comes a day after the luxury group reported better-than-expected sales in the third quarter.</p><p>Which were helped by increased demand in China.</p><p>Rivals Kering, Hermes, Richemont, Burberry and Moncler were up between 5% and 7% in early trade.\u00a0</p><p>Analysts saw LVMH\u2019s results beat as a good sign for continued recovery.</p><p>Highlighting that sales exceeded expectations across all divisions.</p><p>This sales rise at LVMH - a bellwether of fashion, alcohol and retail - represent its first quarter of growth this year.\u00a0</p><p>It said Tuesday that sales in mainland China, a traditional growth driver for the sector, turned positive.</p><p>And that shoppers were responding well to new store experiences.</p><p>Chinese appetite for luxury goods has been hurt by a property crisis.</p><p>It\u2019s clouded a sector which has also seen volatility in the U.S., its key market, due to trade wars bringing economic uncertainty. \u00a0</p><p>But analysts considered the group\u2019s Q3 sales reassuring.</p><p>LVMH's sales in Asia, excluding Japan and dominated by China, made up 28% of annual turnover last year.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: LVMH shares jumped to highs of 14% on Wednesday morning, prompting a sector-wide rally.&nbsp;</p><p>It comes a day after the luxury group reported better-than-expected sales in the third quarter.</p><p>Which were helped by increased demand in China.</p><p>Rivals Kering, Hermes, Richemont, Burberry and Moncler were up between 5% and 7% in early trade.&nbsp;</p><p>Analysts saw LVMH\u2019s results beat as a good sign for continued recovery.</p><p>Highlighting that sales exceeded expectations across all divisions.</p><p>This sales rise at LVMH - a bellwether of fashion, alcohol and retail - represent its first quarter of growth this year.&nbsp;</p><p>It said Tuesday that sales in mainland China, a traditional growth driver for the sector, turned positive.</p><p>And that shoppers were responding well to new store experiences.</p><p>Chinese appetite for luxury goods has been hurt by a property crisis.</p><p>It\u2019s clouded a sector which has also seen volatility in the U.S., its key market, due to trade wars bringing economic uncertainty. &nbsp;</p><p>But analysts considered the group\u2019s Q3 sales reassuring.</p><p>LVMH's sales in Asia, excluding Japan and dominated by China, made up 28% of annual turnover last year.</p></body>",
